Z||000000||Patrick||10-11-1999||06:53 PM||||<BR>As the heading states, Happy Thanksgiving Day !!!<P>In Canada, we get the jump on the Americans by having our Thanksgiving Day a month earlier. This is probably due to the fact that our growing season generally ends sooner.<P>I believe that this is a "New World" tradition. Does anyone know of similar celebrations of the harvest elsewhere in the world?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Patrick||10-12-1999||03:34 PM||||<BR>I guess inquiring about other harvest celebrations around the world was a bit much to ask for in an automotive forum. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just so there's no panic to the south, I want to assure our American friends that a few skinny turkeys have been saved for <B>your</B> Thanksgiving Day next month. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
